.TH CONVERTIBLE-BATTERY-NOTIFY 1 "October 2026" "convertible-power" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
convertible-battery-notify \- charge-limit reminder for laptops without a firmware charge limit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B convertible-battery-notify
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs as a systemd user service (convertible-battery-notify.service). While the battery is charging it
shows one desktop notification, once per charge, when the charge reaches the maximum in
.IR /etc/convertible-power/battery.conf
(default 80%), asking you to unplug. It stays silent when a battery exposes a hardware limit
(charge_control_end_threshold) at or below that value, because the firmware then stops charging by itself.
.PP
The environment variable CONVERTIBLE_POWER_BATTERY_CONF names another configuration file (for testing).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/convertible-power/battery.conf
The maximum and minimum charge.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tlp (8),
.BR upower (1)
